I mean, yes, it is.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.610
Hey, David.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.849
Longtime fan.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.919
You're actually the first person that got
me into podcasting.

00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:19.560
I just wanted to say thank you.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
Thank you.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.609
So love it.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:29.489
I had a question in regards to the piece you
had yesterday in regards to being a hobbyist.

00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:35.010
I was curious on your thoughts on how to guess
make the change from a hobbyist into sort

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:42.379
of an activist, because it is very hard to
get it out of the mindset of just simply looking

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:51.070
at the news or information that may suit you
and applying that to actual change outside

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.219
of that bubble that a person may put themselves
in.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.309
Well, number one, just asking the question
is important, because a lot of people who

00:00:57.309 --> 00:01:01.949
consume political news as entertainment never
ask this question.

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:08.650
They never realize that just like watching
MSNBC doesn't really involve you in politics.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.280
And so I think there's a couple of different
things.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.370
Number one is I recommend everybody at the
macro level don't just consume news.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:21.899
And in fact, I have a very specific and limited
consumption of the day to day news.

00:01:21.899 --> 00:01:25.060
Obviously, I'm producing a show and I'm reacting
to what's happening.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.729
So in doing so, I consume information about
what's going on.

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:35.009
But I actually am focusing more and more of
my time on understanding history and economics

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:36.619
and political philosophy, etc..

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:43.020
So one recommendation I always make is if
you want to take the news and get more involved

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.930
in making change, learn about other things
that will better allow you to interpret what's

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:51.969
going on and contextualize it in history and
within the context of different political

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:53.060
systems, et cetera.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:59.509
But then beyond that, oftentimes what allows
people to go from being political hobbyists

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:04.520
to activists is you can't be an activist on
every issue.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.690
And so figure out what's most important to
you and try to activate there.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:16.340
So if it's climate and local schools, as an
example, figure out how you can get involved

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.080
in wherever you live.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.610
Expanding the infrastructure for transitioning
to clean energy as an example.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.420
Or, you know, I'm just kind of riffing here.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.830
But the idea being you can't just say, well,
I'm a progressive activist and I going to

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.850
get involve everything I pay attention to,
I'm now going to get involved.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:34.850
And it's just not possible.

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:35.850
There's too many things in the world.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.340
So figure out what's most important to you.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:43.500
And then kind of work backwards and say, OK,
where can I most most effectively and at act

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.430
acutely affect some change in these particular
areas?

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.060
I think that that's really the best start.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:53.010
Got it.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.370
So more narrow focus and not being so broad,
we're thinking, because I think that's what

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.240
it comes overwhelming at times.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:05.100
Yeah, a lot of people care about so many different
things that it just becomes too much at once

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.170
to focus on your sphere of influence.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.170
Right.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.170
What can I impact?

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.420
What can I get involved in right now and start.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.310
There you can still pay attention to everything
else that's going on, but try to narrow your

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.560
focus of activism.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.560
Right.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:23.800
I mean, I think right now, I mean, he's in
Texas and right now awards with outstanding

